  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "review-82e033ec3346-1-review-1",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "S2-AC2",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 1,
      "summary": "The S2-AC2 behaviors that are new in this diff have no test at the agreed Lane seam. These are: Lane hidden-ref integration, applying the scoped delta to the working tree, parking on a conflicting local edit with named paths, and the auto-mode settle commit of the applied delta. The seam files tests/unattended-batch-lanes.test.ts and tests/unattended-batch-integration.test.ts are unchanged in the revision, and their verification descriptor is the only evidence the intent names for S2-AC2. Add tests at that seam that pin the cases listed in the trigger.",
      "anchor": "sha256:b508d82d67a39a565aea848697aaee3ebf7b5f644bafdb3f399b514ccb037b18",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "S2-AC2's descriptor runs only tests/unattended-batch-lanes.test.ts and tests/unattended-batch-integration.test.ts. Both are unchanged and call integrateGuardedLaneCommit/integrateLaneCommit with legacy branch names, so they exercise only the legacy ff-only path. The revision tests contain no reference to applyDeltaToWorkingTree, checkDeltaApplies, 'local edits on', commitAppliedDelta or settleCommitSubject. No test makes fastForwardToCandidate (batch_integration.ts) take its hidden-ref branch with a Lane delta. So a regression is invisible to the acceptance check in each of these cases. (a) A Lane delta lands in the working tree while HEAD, branch and index stay put and only refs/imm/batches/<id> moves. (b) A local edit on a delta path makes applyDeltaToWorkingTree return conflicts, so batch_integration_conflict is raised naming those paths and neither the working tree nor the ref changes. (c) Under Git integration auto, commitAppliedDelta commits only the applied paths through the settle commit. (d) A retried apply after an interruption between the apply and the ref move is idempotent. The only related assertion is a status listing in tests/pi-batch-acceptance-integration.test.ts, which does not cover the conflict, named-path or auto-commit outcomes. These cases are a missing test for the acceptance, not a cosmetic gap.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "tests/unattended-batch-integration.test.ts",
          "tests/unattended-batch-lanes.test.ts",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_integration.ts:integrateGuardedLaneCommit",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_integration.ts:fastForwardToCandidate",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_integration.ts:commitAppliedDelta",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_ref.ts:applyDeltaToWorkingTree"
        ],
        "violated": {
          "kind": "acceptance",
          "ref": "S2-AC2"
        }
      },
      "counterevidence": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review-0f45b7927578-1-review-1",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "S2-AC2",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 2,
      "summary": "On a hidden-ref Lane batch, the next reconcile tick's Lane leak-restore treats the delta applied from an integrated Lane as a Lane leak and removes it from the user's working tree, undoing the delivery the hidden-ref integration just wrote.",
      "anchor": "sha256:9f7165f554e6b577ea486ec7f1ce3cda865ddfcbafe83149f9bbf141e65f5d8b",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "A hidden-ref Lane batch (record.branch = refs/imm/batches/<id>) with Git integration manual integrates Lane A, so fastForwardToCandidate applies task-c.txt to the user's working tree and moves the ref. The user's tree has no other dirt. On the next runLaneBatch tick with a persisted record, batch_lanes.ts calls porcelainEntries(root) and gets [{?? task-c.txt}]. restoreProvableLaneLeaks → planLaneLeakRestore → laneOrigin finds a match because the file's blob equals the Lane A commit's blob (record.children[].lane is retained after integration and the Lane branch still holds the commit). The plan is 'provable', so the file is renamed into .imm/state/batches/restores/... and the delivery disappears from the working tree. A modified file (' M') is reverted with `git restore --source=HEAD`. The ref says integrated, but the delivery is gone from the working tree, which contradicts 'each integrated Lane's scoped delta appears in the working tree'. I reproduced this against the revision's runtime files: applyDeltaToWorkingTree wrote task-c.txt, then restoreProvableLaneLeaks returned kind 'restored' and the file was no longer in the tree. batch_preflight.ts also reads this provable plan as clean (statusEntries = []) on resume. The change adds no hidden-ref guard to the leak-restore path. None of the delivered Lane tests cross a second tick after a hidden-ref integration: tests/unattended-batch-integration.test.ts only calls integrateGuardedLaneCommit once, and tests/unattended-batch-lanes.test.ts is unchanged.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_lanes.ts (runLaneBatch: restoreProvableLaneLeaks call on persisted re-entry)",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_leak_restore.ts (planLaneLeakRestore, laneOrigin, restoreProvableLaneLeaks)",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_integration.ts (fastForwardToCandidate hidden branch)",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_ref.ts (applyDeltaToWorkingTree)",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_preflight.ts (projectPreflight: planLaneLeakRestore provable → statusEntries cleared)"
        ],
        "violated": {
          "kind": "acceptance",
          "ref": "S2-AC2"
        }
      },
      "counterevidence": null
    }
  ],
